Subject: Carry the Windows ETW library dependency in the native archive

Base: rusty_v8 v0.106.0 (e9f20a2493883b53cb58b19a2fe761358dd57996),
with V8 at 245ce17ed8483e6bc3de7f668635f46c5bfdd8a0.

V8 enables ETW (Event Tracing for Windows) support on Windows and declares
Advapi32.lib in GN. rusty_v8's print_link_flags() does not forward that
dependency to Cargo consumers. Static archive creation can succeed while
the final executable fails to link EventRegister, EventSetInformation,
EventUnregister, and EventWriteTransfer from etw-jit-win.obj. Do not rely
on incidental linkage from Rust's standard library or another archive
member to supply this dependency.

The Cargo declaration logically belongs in rusty_v8's consumer build.rs:
    println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=dylib=advapi32");
However, this repository distributes archives for the unmodified crates.io
v8 0.106.0 crate. Patching only our build submodule's build.rs would not
change the script downstream consumers run: Cargo link metadata does not
travel inside the archive.

Instead, put a Windows-only pragma in the C++ adapter. It emits a COFF
/DEFAULTLIB:advapi32.lib directive in the adapter object, which the linker
reads when it selects that object from the archive for rusty_v8's API.
The consumer therefore needs no extra link flag. This does not bundle the
Windows library, disable ETW, or change V8's runtime behavior. Non-Windows
compilation is unaffected by the guarded pragma.

Validation: link and run the standalone crates.io rusty_v8 consumer against
the packaged Windows archive without adding Advapi32 in consumer flags or
build scripts. Native compilation alone is not sufficient. The ICU/WasmGC
smoke test validates linking and execution, not ETW event collection.
Remove the patch when the supported downstream crate itself declares the
dependency, or when the archive no longer contains ETW references. An
upstream version bump alone is not evidence that this has been fixed.

Dependency and consumer-link ownership:
https://github.com/denoland/v8/blob/245ce17ed8483e6bc3de7f668635f46c5bfdd8a0/BUILD.gn#L6722
https://github.com/denoland/rusty_v8/blob/v0.106.0/build.rs#L669
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/evntprov/nf-evntprov-eventregister

diff --git a/src/binding.cc b/src/binding.cc
--- a/src/binding.cc
+++ b/src/binding.cc
@@ -33,6 +33,12 @@
 #include "v8/src/objects/objects.h"
 #include "v8/src/objects/smi.h"
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+// GN's system libraries do not propagate through a static archive to Cargo.
+// Keep V8's ETW dependency with the adapter instead of relying on Rust's std.
+#pragma comment(lib, "advapi32.lib")
+#endif
+
 using namespace support;
 
 template <typename T>
